110
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:53,000
Chapter Three: Their Dream

111
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,050


112
00:03:57,530 --> 00:04:01,260
We'll make the 20th century
the Age of Electricity.

113
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:04,520
This is electricity?

114
00:04:05,650 --> 00:04:07,220
This is Seiroku's dream?

115
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:11,750
<i>And now it belongs to me!</i>

116
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:15,030
What the hell is with that little brat?!

117
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:22,670
It was nothing but doodling.

118
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:24,040
I saw it myself!

119
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,750
But the brat created a Full Moon…

120
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,750
Wait. That catalog was a fake, wasn't it?

121
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:32,390
It must be.

122
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:34,000
There must be a real one.

123
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,590
Otherwise, that brat…

124
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,800
Get me some clothes!
We're going to see the brat!

125
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,510
Two <i>hiyashiame</i>!

126
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:45,680
Thank you!

127
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:46,860
Thank you.

128
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:47,770
Thank you.

129
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,130
It's so refreshing.

130
00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:55,380
So this is the famous
steam-cooled <i>hiyashiame</i>!

131
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,400
Good thing we passed the stalls.

132
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,480
The Surugaya <i>yokan</i> is delicious too.

133
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:05,540
He brought it with him to the war
so that he could write this.

134
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:09,750
I'll build all the other ideas
in the catalog too.

135
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:13,000
Then the Age of Electricity…

136
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:16,810
Kihachi-san!

137
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:20,630
Let's celebrate the success
of the Electric Full Moon.

138
00:05:21,150 --> 00:05:22,520
Not right now.

139
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:28,180
We can't offend the deities of food
by letting the <i>hiyashiame</i> get warm.

140
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:34,400
It's sweet, refreshing, and yummy, right?

141
00:05:37,910 --> 00:05:38,910
I suppose.

142
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:43,150
Where's the real catalog, sparky brat?

143
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:43,840
Mizoe-san?

144
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,990
What are you here for, pretty boy?

145
00:05:46,750 --> 00:05:48,160
Get me the real one!

146
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:48,450
Huh?!

147
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:50,680
Find it, Izo!

148
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:52,080
Yes, sir.

149
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:52,330
Hey!

150
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:53,830
Don't hold back!

151
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:55,790
Yosuke-sama?

152
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:56,380
What the…

153
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:57,880
Yosuke-sama!

154
00:05:58,630 --> 00:05:59,920
Let go, you bastards!

155
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:03,180
The exit's that way!

156
00:06:01,350 --> 00:06:03,180
The exit's that way!

157
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:04,980
Don't give me orders!

158
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:08,180
Yosuke, these guys
are probably ex-military.

159
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:10,860
I can't defend you on my own.

160
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,260
Damn you!

161
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:15,070
What's with him?

162
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:16,470
Mommy!

163
00:06:15,590 --> 00:06:16,260
Whoa.

164
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,290
Oh no!

165
00:06:17,290 --> 00:06:19,690
That's dangerous!

166
00:06:19,690 --> 00:06:20,900
My, my…

167
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:21,840
Hey…

168
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,420
Are you okay?

169
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:24,950
Oh, it's that guy!

170
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,450
He's the young master at Nishikiya!

171
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,700
You set those street vendor thugs on us!

172
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:33,990
They were under my command in the war.

173
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:37,130
They said they needed work,
so I found them some.

174
00:06:37,410 --> 00:06:40,170
Don't play dumb!
Why are you getting in my way?

175
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:44,260
Yosuke, you saw the Full Moon, didn't you?

176
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:51,430
Why don't you see
how things go for a little while?

177
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:55,740
Forget it!

178
00:07:02,510 --> 00:07:06,060
Boss! The Young Master…

179
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,910
It's awfully dark in here.

180
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:09,730
Is this shop going un—

181
00:07:09,730 --> 00:07:10,910
Kihachi-san!

182
00:07:10,910 --> 00:07:15,330
Nishikiya is a shop
with a long tradition of Nishijin weaving!

183
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:18,630
Young Master!

184
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,140
Thank you very much.

185
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:24,550
To think trouble has even reached
Momokawa Sake Brewery…

186
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:28,530
What happened to the young proprietor?

187
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:29,640
Even on the way here…

188
00:07:29,990 --> 00:07:31,040
Mommy.

189
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,890
That's the only thing he says.

190
00:07:33,810 --> 00:07:35,770
It's a shameful matter.

191
00:07:36,550 --> 00:07:39,340
The proprietress
who usually runs the business

192
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:41,900
has shut herself in her room lately.

193
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,090
Did something happen?

194
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:50,160
Actually, while the proprietress
was out discussing business,

195
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:54,770
the proprietor collapsed
and passed away before she returned.

196
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:57,380
It's not as if it was her fault.

197
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:00,670
Even so, she's been
in poor spirits ever since.

198
00:08:01,370 --> 00:08:02,240
Inago?

199
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,840
She couldn't be there
when someone close to her died.

200
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:06,720
Oh, Mommy…

201
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,960
I know how she feels!

202
00:08:14,090 --> 00:08:15,130
You can't come in!

203
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:16,810
Ishikiya-san!

204
00:08:17,110 --> 00:08:21,500
Isn't it time you laid off
these outdated craftsmen

205
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,860
and installed our steam looms?

206
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:26,020
If you do, your debt is no more!

207
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:28,400
Then you won't have to close your shop.

208
00:08:28,950 --> 00:08:34,200
As for me, I don't have time to waste
on these matters!

209
00:08:34,550 --> 00:08:36,040
Branch Manager Mizoe.

210
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:38,370
Fancy pants!

211
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:38,370
Sparky brat!

212
00:08:39,110 --> 00:08:40,500
Where's the real catalog?

213
00:08:41,070 --> 00:08:43,900
There's no way you made
a full moon from doodles.

214
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:46,260
You don't have his talent!

215
00:08:45,770 --> 00:08:47,510
Please stop!

216
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:49,630
My honey.

217
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:53,850
I believe I told you to behave
like a proper Mizoe wife.

218
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:58,450
It's not true that Kihachi-san has no talent!

219
00:08:58,450 --> 00:09:00,900
The electric things he makes are amazing!

220
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:05,440
Thanks to Kihachi-san,
I met my mother in Heaven!

221
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,110
What?

222
00:09:06,670 --> 00:09:08,080
Is that true?

223
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:11,670
Rather than someone
with the same voice and build,

224
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:15,410
if she could meet the real proprietor,
I'm sure the proprietress would cheer up!

225
00:09:15,410 --> 00:09:17,080
Yes! No doubt!

226
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:20,280
And then we won't need
steam-powered looms.

227
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:21,450
Right, Young Master?

228
00:09:21,450 --> 00:09:22,290
Daddy!

229
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:26,090
Please! Allow her to see the proprietor!

230
00:09:26,090 --> 00:09:27,060
Please!

231
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:28,670
Please!

232
00:09:27,070 --> 00:09:28,670
Mommy!

233
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:30,120
Huh?

234
00:09:32,070 --> 00:09:34,350
She says she met with the dead?

235
00:09:34,730 --> 00:09:37,090
Just as I thought, the real catalog…

236
00:09:37,090 --> 00:09:40,850
But if the brat made that Full Moon
with advanced electricity…

237
00:09:41,610 --> 00:09:42,590
It can't be.

238
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:50,250
Have someone monitor the boy!

239
00:09:50,250 --> 00:09:50,990
Sir!

240
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,750
A bath?

241
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:57,920
Number nine, the Electric Hot Spring.

242
00:09:57,920 --> 00:10:02,300
Running electricity through the water
makes your body healthier.

243
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:03,370
That's amazing.

244
00:10:03,370 --> 00:10:09,480
Yes. I can't help her to meet the dead,
but this may cheer the proprietress up.

245
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,760
It's like a dream!

246
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:11,800
Kihachi-san?

247
00:10:16,430 --> 00:10:17,850
I can still feel tingling.

248
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:21,910
Forgive me, Kihachi-san.
This is all because of what I said.

249
00:10:21,910 --> 00:10:24,570
Maybe it's a three, not an eight.

250
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:25,800
Let me see.

251
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:26,490
Yes.

252
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:30,190
Which is it?

253
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,050
It's no use.

254
00:10:32,050 --> 00:10:34,920
The ink is too smudged to read properly.

255
00:10:35,370 --> 00:10:39,000
Huh? What about the Electric Hot Spring?

256
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,330
I can't put an elderly person in danger.

257
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:46,040
But then the proprietress
will stay the same.

258
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:48,900
There might be other options, but…

259
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:52,050
You were crying earlier too.

260
00:10:52,990 --> 00:10:56,180
I know how it feels
to lose someone important to you.

261
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:56,860
Kihachi…

262
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,870
Huh? Oh…

263
00:10:59,970 --> 00:11:03,900
What kind of person was your mom, Inago?

264
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:09,440
My mother was…

265
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:14,360
<i>She was very strict
when it came to making sake.</i>

266
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:17,860
<i>But outside the brewery, she was kind</i>

267
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:21,080
<i>and often hugged my older sister and me.</i>

268
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:25,120
<i>The sake my mother made was very popular,</i>

269
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:28,300
<i>and my father
was always busy delivering it.</i>

270
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:32,050
<i>The brewery was also
much livelier than it is now.</i>

271
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:37,300
<i>But then, my mother got sick from soot,</i>

272
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:38,550
<i>and that winter…</i>

273
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:43,680
Even now, I still think about it.

274
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:46,710
I wanted to talk with her more

275
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:50,900
about making sake,
where I want to go on a trip, or…

276
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:54,150
I wanted to talk to her
about so many things.

277
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:56,970
That's why I want
the proprietress to recover

278
00:11:56,970 --> 00:12:00,660
and talk to the young proprietor
and the others as much as possible!

279
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:01,850
Inago…

280
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:03,900
You made the Full Moon!

281
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:07,620
You must be able to help the proprietress
meet the proprietor!

282
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,630
I believe in you, Kihachi-san!

283
00:12:13,630 --> 00:12:15,630
The 20th Century
 Electrical
 Catalog

284
00:12:16,470 --> 00:12:20,510
Meeting someone who's passed away
is impossible, just like I said.

285
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:22,600
But

286
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:27,850
I can't just stand by
when she has nothing but sadness ahead.

287
00:12:27,850 --> 00:12:29,330
Kihachi-san!

288
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:32,190
Okay.

289
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:36,990
I'll arrange for them to meet
and cheer up the proprietress!

290
00:12:37,410 --> 00:12:39,610
Yesterday you said you couldn't do it.

291
00:12:39,610 --> 00:12:40,360
I can't!

292
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,020
What?

293
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:41,910
But I can!

294
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:43,280
Oh, really?

295
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,890
No way. How?

296
00:12:45,410 --> 00:12:46,250
Do you wanna hear?

297
00:12:46,250 --> 00:12:48,060
I wanna hear!

298
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:51,690
According to the Electrical Catalog,
by converting electricity…

299
00:12:51,690 --> 00:12:54,230
I'll do my best too.

300
00:12:54,230 --> 00:12:55,250
I won't give up!

301
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:02,430
Shall we get food on the way home?

302
00:13:02,430 --> 00:13:03,980
I want something steam-grilled.

303
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:06,350
I have to go to Nishikiya-san.

304
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:13,610
<i>Namu Amida Butsu</i>

305
00:13:13,610 --> 00:13:17,110
Madam, please listen
to what I have to say.

306
00:13:17,110 --> 00:13:20,030
<i>Namu Amida Butsu</i>

307
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:29,460
Damn it!

308
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:35,670
How am I supposed to convert
sound vibrations into electricity?

309
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:42,600
If I can use the vibrations
to make a switch…

310
00:13:48,730 --> 00:13:50,980
Please, madam!

311
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:54,400
Please leave me be.

312
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:07,830
It's not transmitting my voice.

313
00:14:08,950 --> 00:14:09,910
This isn't working.

314
00:14:12,750 --> 00:14:16,090
Please, do not concern yourself with me.

315
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:20,460
Sorry for disturbing you.

316
00:14:28,010 --> 00:14:28,630
Huh?

317
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:29,380
<i>Huh?</i>

318
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,390
Carbon changes the electrical resistance…

319
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,590
Okay.

320
00:14:49,590 --> 00:14:51,450
Now I can make it work.

321
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,720
Please come out of your room, madam.

322
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:04,250
If you could, please!

323
00:15:10,230 --> 00:15:11,530
Is everything ready?

324
00:15:11,530 --> 00:15:12,490
Yes.

325
00:15:12,490 --> 00:15:16,060
We just have to wait
for Inago to bring her here.

326
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,200
You're here again?

327
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:22,570
I want to stay here
and keep praying for the one I lost.

328
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:26,070
Everyone is waiting for you, madam.

329
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,830
Why are you so concerned with me?

330
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:33,120
What does it have to do with you?

331
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:36,830
I don't want you to have any regrets!

332
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:40,670
I already feel regret every day!

333
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:44,630
I lost my mother three years ago!

334
00:15:46,990 --> 00:15:49,640
There were so many things
I wanted to talk to her about.

335
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:55,720
But I was still a child
and didn't understand anything.

336
00:15:55,720 --> 00:16:00,080
By the time I finally understood,
I could no longer meet her.

337
00:16:02,350 --> 00:16:03,030
Madam!

338
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:08,240
Please show your face and speak lots
with the young proprietor and the others!

339
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:13,270
I don't want you or the young proprietor
to have any regrets!

340
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:14,620
Even a little bit is fine!

341
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:16,550
Please!

342
00:16:22,010 --> 00:16:25,460
What are you trying to say?

343
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,170
Madam!

344
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:31,300
I suppose you don't want any more regrets.

345
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:32,680
Thank you so much.

346
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:36,530
So there are still
tenacious people like you around.

347
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:38,440
Forgive me.

348
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:40,360
It's fine.

349
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:43,300
Thanks to you, I can leave my room
for the first time in a while.

350
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:45,230
I'm glad.

351
00:16:45,230 --> 00:16:47,730
Now you'll be able to meet the proprietor.

352
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:49,820
What did you just say?

353
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:53,060
There's a machine I'd like to show you.

354
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:55,130
You're not saying I can use it to…

355
00:16:55,130 --> 00:16:58,160
Yes! You can speak with the proprietor.

356
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:01,810
With him? Something like that exists?

357
00:17:01,810 --> 00:17:03,950
Yes. Let's go!

358
00:17:03,950 --> 00:17:07,530
Yes. Let's go right away.

359
00:17:07,530 --> 00:17:07,970
Ouch!

360
00:17:07,970 --> 00:17:09,070
Madam!

361
00:17:09,070 --> 00:17:11,970
I'm stiff from being shut in so long.

362
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:15,310
Don't worry. I'll help you.

363
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,690
Madam, a little slower!

364
00:17:19,690 --> 00:17:21,310
Madam!

365
00:17:24,430 --> 00:17:26,940
Ouch! My leg cramped up.

366
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:28,110
Inako-san!

367
00:17:28,110 --> 00:17:31,030
Yes, madam…

368
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,470
Whoa!

369
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:37,990
Please sit over here.

370
00:17:54,330 --> 00:17:56,070
Place your ear here.

371
00:17:56,070 --> 00:17:58,590
Speak into this when you're ready.

372
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,400
<i>Chiyo.</i>

373
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:14,480
Is that you, dear?

374
00:18:20,590 --> 00:18:24,750
You departed so suddenly, and I…

375
00:18:26,390 --> 00:18:28,930
I worked very hard

376
00:18:28,930 --> 00:18:33,060
because we promised to make this
the best shop in Kyoto.

377
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:34,380
<i>Yes.</i>

378
00:18:35,570 --> 00:18:38,180
I can't do it alone.

379
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,270
I wore myself out.

380
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:47,190
And before I knew it,
the shop began to fall apart.

381
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,970
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

382
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:58,040
You don't have to push yourself.

383
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:03,690
Everyone is sad when you're not around.

384
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:35,650
Dear…

385
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:40,510
Never mind. I'll keep trying after all.

386
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:45,250
This shop is full
of precious memories with you.

387
00:19:46,770 --> 00:19:48,010
<i>Thank you.</i>

388
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:52,750
Thank you, dear.

389
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:55,510
Sir!

390
00:20:01,590 --> 00:20:02,990
My goodness.

391
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:05,770
Look at the state of this store.

392
00:20:07,470 --> 00:20:09,310
Seems you can't manage without me.

393
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,190
Akira! Where's Akira?

394
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,590
Mother!

395
00:20:19,070 --> 00:20:22,180
Hurry up and open the store, all of you.

396
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:22,780
Yes!

397
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:22,780
Yes!

398
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:27,320
Thank you, Inako-san.

399
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:28,150
Of course.

400
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:31,210
Come on, get to work!

401
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:33,000
Did you see that, Inago?

402
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:37,940
Yes. Talking to someone
who has passed away is like a dream!

403
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:38,670
Huh?

404
00:20:38,670 --> 00:20:41,190
I'd like to talk to my mom too.

405
00:20:41,190 --> 00:20:42,430
That's impossible.

406
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,430
Huh? Why?

407
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:47,270
The young proprietor was the one talking.

408
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,380
"Electric Telepathy"!

409
00:20:49,380 --> 00:20:51,770
You can talk to people even from far away.

410
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:55,610
Huh? So you didn't summon
the proprietor's spirit?

411
00:20:55,610 --> 00:20:56,690
Are you serious?

412
00:20:59,030 --> 00:21:01,580
<i>Come on, I already explained!</i>

413
00:20:59,030 --> 00:21:01,580
<i>Come on, I already explained!</i>

414
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:02,690
Jeez!

415
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:04,690
Still,

416
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:08,340
the proprietress is feeling better.

417
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:11,330
It's all thanks to your help, Kihachi-san.

418
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,600
Thank you very much!

419
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:16,630
It was nothing.

420
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:20,340
The amazing thing is Big Brother Seiroku's notes…

421
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:18,690
That's enough!

422
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:24,810
Yosuke-sama.

423
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:27,680
I have the surveillance report.

424
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:30,890
The ghost of Nishikiya's
previous proprietor appeared,

425
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:35,150
and they spoke for a few minutes
with a device similar to a phonograph.

426
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,660
There's no mistake.

427
00:21:46,650 --> 00:21:50,620
That brat has the real catalog.

428
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:55,420
Your younger brother has made
the Electrical Catalog a reality again.

429
00:22:12,020 --> 00:22:17,460
Only you and I should know
the catalog's true secrets.

430
00:22:18,590 --> 00:22:19,740
Isn't that so?

431
00:22:27,170 --> 00:22:28,340
Seiroku.

432
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:33,680
I will get my hands on the real catalog.

433
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:38,340
And then, I promise that we'll chase
our dreams together again.

434
